# Corresponding-source disposition of everything the product distributes in binary or data form.
# One row per path of provenance.psv that is an artifact (a path starting with "./"), an embedded
# third-party library ("embedded:"), or a group of image rows (the last two rows, which use a
# trailing * as a wildcard). tests/test_sbom_completeness.sh requires that every such row of
# provenance.psv resolves to a row here, with a valid disposition, and that a row named
# source-recorded points at an id that exists in corresponding_source.psv.
#
# This file states what the records hold. It is not a legal conclusion. Which source the release
# assets hold is stated in SOURCE-OFFER.md and source-assets/SOURCE-INDEX.md.
#
# disposition:
#   source-recorded          corresponding_source.psv holds a row (named in the id field) that pins the
#                            exact source revision or checksum and, where known, how it was built
#   binary-only-no-source-record
#                            a binary or data file supplied under its own licence agreement; no
#                            source row exists and none is offered here
#   source-asset             the corresponding source (or relink or build material) is a release asset of
#                            version 1.0.0, named in the id field and listed with its checksum in
#                            source-assets/ASSETS.psv
#   upstream-reference-only  the component is described in provenance.psv by an upstream location,
#                            version and checksum or commit; its license does not require source to be
#                            provided with the binary, so no archive is included in the release assets
#
# path | disposition | id | notes
./morse.ko | source-asset | morse-driver-source-2.1.0.tar.gz | driver source (with the rate-control code); build material in kernel-module-build-material-1.0.0.tar.xz, kernel-prep.sh, linux-6.18.58.tar.xz, haos-operating-system-18.4.tar.gz and buildroot-d2b75e05.tar.gz
./dot11ah.ko | source-asset | morse-driver-source-2.1.0.tar.gz | driver source (with the rate-control code); build material in kernel-module-build-material-1.0.0.tar.xz, kernel-prep.sh, linux-6.18.58.tar.xz, haos-operating-system-18.4.tar.gz and buildroot-d2b75e05.tar.gz
./hostapd_s1g | source-asset | hostap-source-2.1.0.tar.gz | hostap source; relink material in hostapd-relink-material-1.0.0.tar.xz; build script source-offer/build-hostapd.sh
./hostapd_cli_s1g | source-asset | hostap-source-2.1.0.tar.gz | hostap source; relink material in hostapd-relink-material-1.0.0.tar.xz; build script source-offer/build-hostapd.sh
./hostapd_s1g.conf | source-asset | hostap-source-2.1.0.tar.gz | configuration template from the same repository
./mm8108b2-rl.bin | binary-only-no-source-record | none | chip firmware supplied under the licence agreement named in provenance.psv; no source row
./bcf/bcf_boardtype_0807.bin | binary-only-no-source-record | none | board data file supplied under the licence agreement named in provenance.psv; no source row
embedded:openssl | source-recorded | static-lib-openssl | statically linked into hostapd_s1g; Apache-2.0, so no archive is included; the release tarball and its checksum are pinned in source-offer/build-hostapd.sh
embedded:glibc | source-asset | glibc-2.41-5dd252cf.tar.gz | statically linked into both executables; relink material in hostapd-relink-material-1.0.0.tar.xz
embedded:libnl | source-asset | libnl-3.11.0.tar.gz | statically linked into hostapd_s1g; relink material in hostapd-relink-material-1.0.0.tar.xz
embedded:libgcc | source-recorded | static-lib-libgcc | statically linked into the executables under the GCC Runtime Library Exception; no GCC 13.4.0 source in the assets (the Alpine gcc source for the base image libgcc is)
embedded:mmrc | source-asset | morse-driver-source-2.1.0.tar.gz | compiled into morse.ko; the rate-control submodule is filled in inside the driver archive
image-component:jemalloc | upstream-reference-only | none | shared library installed by the base image; its license (the text of COPYING, two numbered conditions and a disclaimer, equal to BSD-2-Clause in substance) does not require source; the upstream tag is named in provenance.psv
image-component:* | upstream-reference-only | none | programs and files installed by the base image or by this add-on under permissive licenses (s6 family ISC, tempio Apache-2.0, bashio MIT) or data (the CA bundle, whose package source is in the Alpine asset, and pip.conf); upstream location named in provenance.psv; not separately included in the release assets
image-package:alpine-baselayout | source-asset | alpine-3.23-copyleft-sources-1.0.0.tar | source is in the alpine-baselayout-3.7.2-r0 directory of the Alpine asset
